# Forces the real flash-size Kconfig symbol for the idf-family envs whose
# board_build.flash_size = 4MB. Confirmed on real ESP32-S3 hardware
# (2026-08-21): PlatformIO's board_build.flash_size setting does not
# propagate into the compiled sdkconfig for Arduino-as-IDF-component builds
# -- it silently falls back to ESP-IDF's raw default (2MB) regardless of
# what board_build.flash_size claims, which esptool then flags at upload
# time ("Flash memory size mismatch") and which corrupts flash-encrypted
# boots (encryption is address-dependent, so a wrong size assumption
# produces garbage reads -- this is what caused the "invalid header"
# boot-loop on env:idf-secure-s3). Fix: set the Kconfig symbol explicitly
# instead of relying on board_build.flash_size alone.
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE_4MB=y
